s owned by other users. this exposes sensitive conversation data and allows unauthorized manipulation of ai-generated outputs."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-0598","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.6","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.6"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-0598","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-0598","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-0598","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-283","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-283"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-0598","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-0598","predicate":"vendor","object":"Red Hat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44187","predicate":"assigner","object":"redhat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"redhat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44187","predicate":"cvss-base-score","object":"3.3","source":"cve","object_type":"number","object_canonical":"3.3"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44187","predicate":"cvss-severity","object":"LOW","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"low"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44187","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-07-22T12:06:50.258Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-22t12:06:50.258z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44187","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-07-22T16:02:42.074Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-22t16:02:42.074z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44187","predicate":"description","object":"A flaw was found in the Ansible Lightspeed extension for Visual Studio Code. This vulnerability allows an attacker with local access to the workstation, or malware running with the user's privileges, to read the Google Gemini API key. The extension insecurely stores the API key in plain text within the user's configuration file and writes it to output log files. This information disclosure can lead to the attacker obtaining the API credential and potentially consuming the user's API quota.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a flaw was found in the ansible lightspeed extension for visual studio code. this vulnerability allows an attacker with local access to the workstation, or malware running with the user's privileges, to read the google gemini api key. the extension insecurely stores the api key in plain text within the user's configuration file and writes it to output log files. this information disclosure can lead to the attacker obtaining the api credential and potentially consuming the user's api quota."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44187","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44187","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44187","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-256","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-256"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44187","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44187","predicate":"vendor","object":"Red Hat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"affects-cpe","object":"cpe:/a:redhat:ansible_automation_platform:2.6::el9","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"cpe:/a:redhat:ansible_automation_platform:2.6::el9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"affects-cpe","object":"cpe:/a:redhat:ansible_automation_platform:2.7::el9","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"cpe:/a:redhat:ansible_automation_platform:2.7::el9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"assigner","object":"redhat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"redhat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"cvss-base-score","object":"5.3","source":"cve","object_type":"number","object_canonical":"5.3"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"cvss-severity","object":"MEDIUM","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"medium"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-06-15T08:36:06.652Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-06-15t08:36:06.652z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-08-20T15:14:03.037Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-08-20t15:14:03.037z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"description","object":"A flaw was found in Ansible Lightspeed. This vulnerability, related to insufficient session expiration, allows a remote attacker to maintain persistent access to the Ansible Lightspeed instance. If an attacker exfiltrates a valid OAuth (Open Authorization) access token before a user logs out, they can continue to authenticate and access sensitive data. This is because the application fails to invalidate the token on the backend, leaving it valid until its natural expiration. This can lead to unauthorized read access to Ansible resources such as inventories, playbooks, and configuration data.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a flaw was found in ansible lightspeed. this vulnerability, related to insufficient session expiration, allows a remote attacker to maintain persistent access to the ansible lightspeed instance. if an attacker exfiltrates a valid oauth (open authorization) access token before a user logs out, they can continue to authenticate and access sensitive data. this is because the application fails to invalidate the token on the backend, leaving it valid until its natural expiration. this can lead to unauthorized read access to ansible resources such as inventories, playbooks, and configuration data."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.6","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.6"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.7","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.7"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-613","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-613"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44188","predicate":"vendor","object":"Red Hat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44189","predicate":"assigner","object":"redhat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"redhat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44189","predicate":"cvss-base-score","object":"7.8","source":"cve","object_type":"number","object_canonical":"7.8"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44189","predicate":"cvss-severity","object":"HIGH","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"high"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44189","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-07-22T12:06:36.571Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-22t12:06:36.571z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44189","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-07-22T12:19:09.393Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-22t12:19:09.393z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44189","predicate":"description","object":"A flaw was found in the Visual Studio Code Ansible Lightspeed extension's AnsiblePlaybookRunProvider. This command injection vulnerability allows an attacker to craft a malicious playbook filename containing special characters. When a victim runs the playbook, these characters are not properly sanitized, leading to the execution of arbitrary code with the privileges of the user running VS Code. This could result in a full system compromise, including the exfiltration of sensitive data, modification of project files, and permanent data loss.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a flaw was found in the visual studio code ansible lightspeed extension's ansibleplaybookrunprovider. this command injection vulnerability allows an attacker to craft a malicious playbook filename containing special characters. when a victim runs the playbook, these characters are not properly sanitized, leading to the execution of arbitrary code with the privileges of the user running vs code. this could result in a full system compromise, including the exfiltration of sensitive data, modification of project files, and permanent data loss."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44189","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44189","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44189","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-88","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-88"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44189","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44189","predicate":"vendor","object":"Red Hat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44190","predicate":"assigner","object":"redhat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"redhat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44190","predicate":"cvss-base-score","object":"7.8","source":"cve","object_type":"number","object_canonical":"7.8"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44190","predicate":"cvss-severity","object":"HIGH","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"high"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44190","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-07-22T12:06:42.591Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-22t12:06:42.591z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44190","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-07-23T13:50:44.922Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-23t13:50:44.922z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44190","predicate":"description","object":"A flaw was found in the Ansible Lightspeed Visual Studio Code extension. This Command Injection vulnerability (CWE-78) allows a remote attacker to execute unauthorized commands on a user's system. The issue occurs because the `ansible.python.activationScript` setting, intended for a virtual environment activation script, does not properly validate user input as a file path. If a user opens or executes a specially crafted project, an attacker could exploit this to gain complete control over the user's system with the privileges of the Visual Studio Code application.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a flaw was found in the ansible lightspeed visual studio code extension. this command injection vulnerability (cwe-78) allows a remote attacker to execute unauthorized commands on a user's system. the issue occurs because the `ansible.python.activationscript` setting, intended for a virtual environment activation script, does not properly validate user input as a file path. if a user opens or executes a specially crafted project, an attacker could exploit this to gain complete control over the user's system with the privileges of the visual studio code application."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44190","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44190","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44190","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-78","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-78"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44190","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44190","predicate":"vendor","object":"Red Hat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44191","predicate":"assigner","object":"redhat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"redhat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44191","predicate":"cvss-base-score","object":"7.8","source":"cve","object_type":"number","object_canonical":"7.8"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44191","predicate":"cvss-severity","object":"HIGH","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"high"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44191","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-07-22T12:11:29.899Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-22t12:11:29.899z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44191","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-07-22T18:48:19.980Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-22t18:48:19.980z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44191","predicate":"description","object":"A flaw was found in the Visual Studio Code Ansible Lightspeed extension. This command injection vulnerability (CWE-78) arises from improper handling of the ansible.executionEnvironment.containerOptions and ansible.executionEnvironment.volumeMounts settings, allowing an attacker to inject shell separators. This can be triggered automatically during Language Server initialization or manually when executing a playbook. Successful exploitation leads to remote code execution (RCE) on the victim's machine with the privileges of the Visual Studio Code user, potentially resulting in a complete system compromise.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a flaw was found in the visual studio code ansible lightspeed extension. this command injection vulnerability (cwe-78) arises from improper handling of the ansible.executionenvironment.containeroptions and ansible.executionenvironment.volumemounts settings, allowing an attacker to inject shell separators. this can be triggered automatically during language server initialization or manually when executing a playbook. successful exploitation leads to remote code execution (rce) on the victim's machine with the privileges of the visual studio code user, potentially resulting in a complete system compromise."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44191","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44191","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44191","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-78","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-78"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44191","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44191","predicate":"vendor","object":"Red Hat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44192","predicate":"assigner","object":"redhat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"redhat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44192","predicate":"cvss-base-score","object":"6.6","source":"cve","object_type":"number","object_canonical":"6.6"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44192","predicate":"cvss-severity","object":"MEDIUM","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"medium"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44192","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-07-22T12:06:48.859Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-22t12:06:48.859z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44192","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-07-22T13:05:03.058Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-22t13:05:03.058z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44192","predicate":"description","object":"A flaw was found in the Ansible Lightspeed Model Context Protocol (MCP) server. This vulnerability, known as path traversal, allows an attacker to manipulate an AI agent through indirect prompt injection. By doing so, the attacker can cause the server to write files to unauthorized locations on the user's system. This can result in the exposure of sensitive host information and enable the attacker to execute malicious commands, potentially leading to a full system compromise.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a flaw was found in the ansible lightspeed model context protocol (mcp) server. this vulnerability, known as path traversal, allows an attacker to manipulate an ai agent through indirect prompt injection. by doing so, the attacker can cause the server to write files to unauthorized locations on the user's system. this can result in the exposure of sensitive host information and enable the attacker to execute malicious commands, potentially leading to a full system compromise."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44192","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-44192","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"C